WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:06.206
"How to Control the Muscle Loss Side Effects
(Like “Ozempic Face”) of GLP-1 Drugs"

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.177
GLP-1 type drugs, like Ozempic,

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:13.380
function by making patients
feel fuller, eat less,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.549
and hence, lose weight.

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:18.218
However, an important
but often overlooked factor

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.953
in these studies
of these kinds of drugs

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:23.824
relates to the type of weight
that’s lost.

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:26.193
Typically, when people
who are obese lose weight,

00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:28.695
the decrease
in their fat-free mass,

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.364
meaning essentially
their lean mass,

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:31.798
including their muscles,

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.600
usually represents
about 25 percent

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.002
of their total weight loss.

00:00:35.002 --> 00:00:37.537
So, for every 4 pounds (2 kg)
lost on the scale,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.374
one of those pounds is not fat.

00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:41.508
But on drugs like Ozempic,

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.344
as much as 40 percent
of the total weight lost

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:47.848
is that lean mass, nearly half
the pounds you’re losing.

00:00:47.848 --> 00:00:50.317
Those on Ozempic
or tirzepatide,

00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:53.220
a newer GLP-1 drug
sold as Zepbound,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.656
lost about 14 pounds (6 kg)
of lean mass,

00:00:55.656 --> 00:00:59.393
about one eighth of all
the lean mass in their body.

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:01.628
That’s worse than the amount
of lean mass you lose

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:03.463
when you have
esophageal cancer,

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.732
or head and neck cancer.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.335
Now, some people paid
by the pharma companies

00:01:08.335 --> 00:01:09.970
that make GLP-1-type drugs

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.472
question whether the amount
of muscle mass loss

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.241
is clinically relevant.

00:01:14.241 --> 00:01:17.277
But these drugs cause
such rapid and significant loss

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.946
of lean mass,
that it’s comparable

00:01:18.946 --> 00:01:23.216
to how much you’d lose
over a decade or more of aging.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:26.353
The drug industry consultants
argue that even if 40 percent

00:01:26.353 --> 00:01:28.255
of the weight lost
is lean mass,

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:30.924
that still means the majority,
60 percent, is fat;

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.160
so, you end up
with a better fat-to-lean ratio,

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.494
in the end.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.763
But that’s just
on the first go-around.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.399
Remember, most people
don’t stick to these drugs

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.567
for more than a few months,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.002
either because
they can’t keep paying

00:01:42.002 --> 00:01:43.236
a thousand bucks a month
for them,

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.505
or they don’t want to put up
with all the side effects,

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:49.242
or deal with drug shortages,
or run out of refills.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.211
And when you stop these drugs,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:54.381
we know the lost body fat
piles on back,

00:01:54.381 --> 00:01:55.115
but there’s a concern

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.684
that any lost muscle mass
may not;

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.555
so, you then actually end up
fatter in the end.

00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:03.724
This kind of weight cycling
has been associated

00:02:03.724 --> 00:02:05.692
with extra fat deposition
on the body,

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.427
especially around the middle.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:10.297
Using the gold-standard method,
MRI,

00:02:10.297 --> 00:02:13.166
to directly visualize
muscle mass,

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.068
researchers found
that the more times

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.570
people cycle their weight,

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.673
the worse their body composition
appears to get.

00:02:19.673 --> 00:02:21.708
The profound level
of lean mass loss

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.344
associated
with GLP-1 weight-loss drugs

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.580
would be expected
to have deleterious impacts

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.882
on health outcomes,
including increased frailty

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:31.852
and perhaps greater
long-term mortality risk,

00:02:31.852 --> 00:02:34.621
though, this concern
remains theoretical,

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:38.091
since any such long-term data
have yet to be published.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.927
The good news is there’s
something we can do about it.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.330
Exercise, particularly
resistance exercise,

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.464
like weight training,

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.733
can cut in half or more
the proportion

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.202
of fat-free mass that is lost.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.670
Check this out:

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.140
Based on half a dozen studies
of caloric restriction

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.275
for weight loss
(like portion control),

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:58.578
and the same calorie restriction
plus resistance exercise,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.013
you can see that it appears

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:04.117
the non-exercising group
lost more weight.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.886
You can guess why, though,

00:03:05.886 --> 00:03:07.921
because without
the resistance exercise,

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.856
they lost more lean mass,

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.325
whereas the exercising group
lost nine pounds (4 kg)

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.862
apparently without losing
any lean mass.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:19.366
Supervised resistance training
interventions,

00:03:19.366 --> 00:03:21.768
up to a few times a week
for more than 10 weeks,

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:24.371
where all major muscle groups
are worked,

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:27.040
can add a few extra pounds
of lean mass.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.077
More with weights than cardio,
more when younger,

00:03:30.077 --> 00:03:31.978
and more in men than women.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.915
Collectively, this evidence
supports resistance training

00:03:34.915 --> 00:03:37.717
as an effective approach
to, at the very least,

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.187
help mitigate
the decrease in lean mass;

00:03:40.187 --> 00:03:43.890
so, programs such as these
should be adopted without delay

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.360
in patients embarking
on Ozempic-type therapy.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.629
What about "Ozempic face"?

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.631
The term has consumed the media

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.500
with the medication’s
rising popularity

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.735
and describes rapid weight loss
in the face

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.971
that leaves
a distorted appearance.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:01.775
And I’d never even heard
of Ozempic butt.

00:04:01.775 --> 00:04:05.612
Media reports have linked
the drug to facial aging,

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.848
but perhaps it’s not so much
the medication

00:04:07.848 --> 00:04:09.816
as much as the potent
weight-loss effects

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.485
that leave a sagging appearance

00:04:11.485 --> 00:04:13.620
due to the loss of fat
in the face.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.789
While this seems logical,

00:04:15.789 --> 00:04:18.024
the explanation cannot
fully account

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.560
for the markedly accelerated
facial aging

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.096
seen in GLP-1 drug patients.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:26.066
The premature facial aging
and altered skin health

00:04:26.066 --> 00:04:28.502
appears to be multifactorial,

00:04:28.502 --> 00:04:30.937
involving not only the loss
of fat in the face,

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:33.240
but an effect on stem cells
and the production

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.543
and secretion of hormonal
and metabolic factors.

00:04:36.543 --> 00:04:39.613
These changes compromise
the structural integrity

00:04:39.613 --> 00:04:41.481
and barrier function
of the skin

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:45.252
and may lead to diminished
facial muscle mass as well,

00:04:45.252 --> 00:04:48.889
further exacerbating
the appearance of aging.

00:04:48.889 --> 00:04:52.592
Another side effect of rapid
weight loss is gallstones,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.262
which is not limited
to GLP-1 drugs.

00:04:55.262 --> 00:04:57.130
Shedding
all that excess cholesterol

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.765
stored in your fat cells

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:02.102
can lead to it crystallizing
in your bile like rock candy,

00:05:02.102 --> 00:05:04.004
forming gallstones.

00:05:04.004 --> 00:05:05.872
Something else to be
cognizant of,

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:07.140
but in a way,

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.743
both the muscle loss
and gallstones

00:05:09.743 --> 00:05:11.645
may just be signs
of how effective

00:05:11.645 --> 00:05:13.780
these drugs can be
for losing weight.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:15.849
In my last video,

00:05:15.849 --> 00:05:17.651
I talked
about the common side effects,

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:20.754
but as semaglutide’s
popularity soars,

00:05:20.754 --> 00:05:23.957
rare but serious adverse effects
are emerging.

00:05:23.957 --> 00:05:27.260
Like, what about possible
thyroid cancer, pancreatitis,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.563
kidney problems, depression,
or suicidal thoughts?

00:05:29.563 --> 00:05:32.766
I’ll cover all those next.

